1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,230
Going to the gym can be something that many people find a gruelling experience.
去健身房对很多人来说可能是一种折磨人的（gruelling）经历。

2
00:00:07,230 --> 00:00:13,380
It takes time and effort, it often hurts, and it can be extremely tedious.
这需要时间和努力，而且常常会让人感到疼痛，还可能极其无聊（tedious）。

3
00:00:13,380 --> 00:00:19,250
Most weight-related exercises are a combination of sets and reps.
大多数与举重相关的锻炼是组数和次数的结合。

4
00:00:19,250 --> 00:00:33,250
In order to see any significant change from any one exercise, it will probably need to be repeated six to eight times, for a minimum of three sets, for about three months.
为了从任何一项锻炼中看到明显的变化，可能需要重复六到八次，至少做三组，持续大约三个月。

5
00:00:33,250 --> 00:00:35,460
Then there's cardio.
然后还有有氧运动（cardio）。

6
00:00:35,460 --> 00:00:42,340
For some, there's nothing more boring than endless miles spent running on a treadmill.
对有些人来说，没有什么比在跑步机（treadmill）上无休止地跑上数英里更无聊的了。

7
00:00:42,340 --> 00:00:50,480
But what if there were a way to alleviate the boredom of exercise while still getting a good work out?
但是，如果有一种方法可以在仍然进行良好锻炼的同时减轻（alleviate）锻炼的无聊感呢？

8
00:00:50,480 --> 00:00:54,480
Luckily for us, there’s virtual reality.
幸运的是，我们有虚拟现实技术。

9
00:00:54,480 --> 00:01:06,320
In the past, “playing video games was a sedentary experience,” says Jo Stauffer of the VR Health Institute, “but VR changes all of that".
过去，“玩电子游戏是一种久坐不动的（sedentary）体验，”虚拟现实健康研究所（VR Health Institute）的乔・斯托弗（Jo Stauffer）说，“但虚拟现实改变了这一切。”

10
00:01:06,320 --> 00:01:12,610
He says that the room-scale experience engages your body in full.
他说，空间定位体验能让你的身体完全参与（engages）进来。

11
00:01:12,610 --> 00:01:16,920
Many VR games are played while standing.
许多虚拟现实游戏是站着玩的。

12
00:01:16,920 --> 00:01:24,390
In order to play properly, the player is forced to move around swinging their arms or using their legs.
为了玩好游戏，玩家不得不四处移动，挥舞手臂或使用双腿。

13
00:01:24,390 --> 00:01:33,460
After an hour of this on a regular enough basis, it’s not surprising that many people unexpectedly find themselves a little fitter.
如果经常这样玩上一个小时，很多人意外地发现自己更健康一点也就不足为奇了。

14
00:01:33,460 --> 00:01:46,560
There are already a number of virtual reality games which, deliberately or not, result in their player ‘getting a good sweat on’ if played for enough time.
已经有许多虚拟现实游戏，不管是不是有意为之，如果玩的时间足够长，都会让玩家“出一身汗”。

15
00:01:46,560 --> 00:01:56,500
For example, there’s a first person shooter which forces the player to sidestep, duck and dodge incoming projectiles.
例如，有一款第一人称射击游戏，迫使玩家侧步走（sidestep）、弯腰躲避（duck）和闪避（dodge）飞来的投射物。

16
00:01:56,500 --> 00:01:57,860
That’s cardio.
这就是有氧运动。

17
00:01:57,860 --> 00:02:07,490
Or there’s a music game which forces players to shadowbox in order to hit the notes – that’s an upper-body workout.
或者有一款音乐游戏，迫使玩家做空拳训练（shadowbox）以便击中音符——这是一种上半身锻炼。

18
00:02:07,490 --> 00:02:14,670
The potential for VR to help people get fit has been noticed by one company.
虚拟现实帮助人们健身的潜力已经被一家公司注意到了。

19
00:02:14,670 --> 00:02:18,960
They want to take the whole experience into the gym.
他们想把这种体验引入健身房。

20
00:02:18,960 --> 00:02:26,950
They are making a bespoke resistance machine, designed to be used in combination with a VR headset.
他们正在制造一种定制的（bespoke）阻力机器，设计成与虚拟现实头戴设备结合使用。

21
00:02:26,950 --> 00:02:35,670
Players challenge a virtual opponent in a series of games, which results in a 30-minute full-body work out.
玩家在一系列游戏中挑战虚拟对手，这会带来一次30分钟的全身锻炼。

22
00:02:35,670 --> 00:02:46,140
However, the cost of the equipment is expensive and there are safety concerns to be worked out, says J P Gownder from the consultancy Forrester.
然而，咨询公司佛罗斯特咨询公司（Forrester）的J・P・高恩德（J P Gownder）说，设备的成本很高，而且还有一些安全问题需要解决。

23
00:02:46,140 --> 00:02:49,840
So don’t hang up your gym shorts just yet.
所以，先别急着把你的健身短裤收起来。

24
00:02:49,840 --> 00:02:59,280
Although it’s early days, for those of us who struggle to overcome the tedium of exercise, a new solution could be coming.
尽管还为时尚早，但对于我们这些努力克服锻炼乏味感的人来说，一种新的解决方案可能即将到来。

25
00:02:59,280 --> 00:03:09,780
And a world where a person can exercise and have fun at the same time might be something that many people would want – virtual or not.
而且，一个人们可以同时锻炼和享受乐趣的世界可能是许多人所向往的——不管是不是虚拟的。
